<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lithuanian Crusade</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1283–1422</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-crusades">Northern Crusades</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lithuanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a> was the series of campaigns by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> and the Livonian Order against the pagan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a> from the late thirteenth century. The orders raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> nearly every year, and Lithuania struck back into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a>. The crusade lost its purpose after Lithuania's Christianisation in 1387 and ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-melno">Treaty of Melno</a> in 1422.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lithuanian-crusade.jpg" alt="Lithuanian Crusade" width="320" height="177" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lietuviai_kovoja_su_vokie%C4%8Diais.Lithuanians_fighting_Teutonic_Knights_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
